    "role": "Qliphothic Catastrophe (Gamchicoth — Greater)",
    "tier": 4,
    "factionId": "",
    "notes": "<p>What happens when the impulse to grow is given infinite fuel: a sprawling, amorphous pile of glistening flesh — dozens of mouths, clusters of mismatched eyes, edges always bubbling outward in pseudopods. It may have started as an organism, a town, an ecosystem. Now it is a walking engine of absorption leaving a mutated wasteland behind it. Less a creature than a biological verdict.</p><p><strong>Qliphah:</strong> Gamchicoth, the Tumults — the Hull of Chesed. Growth as devourer of form.</p><p><em>Mal's note: 'Do not name it. People who name it start calling it “she”. People who call it “she” walk toward it.'</em></p>",
